&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;About Wolt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;At Wolt, we create technology that brings joy, simplicity and earnings to the neighborhoods of the world. In 2014 we started with delivery of restaurant food. Now we’re building the delivery of (almost) everything and you’ll find us in over 500 cities in 30 countries around the world. In 2022 we joined forces with DoorDash and together we keep on dreaming big and expanding across the globe.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Working at Wolt isn’t always easy, but it’s definitely exciting. Here you’ll learn more, build more, and ship more than in most other companies. You’ll be challenged a lot, but also have a lot of fun on the way. So, if you’re a self-starter with drive and entrepreneurial spirit, this could be the ride of your life.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Merchant EMEA Engineering builds the technology that helps merchants join, grow, and operate successfully across our markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our organization brings together the strengths of Wolt and Deliveroo and supports merchants across 37 countries. We work across the merchant journey, including onboarding, business growth and support, analytics and recommendations, menu and order management, integrations, and merchant applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our teams sit close to the business. Rather than primarily building foundational platforms, we build products and features on top of our existing platforms to solve real merchant and market needs, including local business requirements, growth opportunities, and operational challenges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📍This open role is based in our tech hubs in &lt;strong&gt;Helsinki&lt;/strong&gt; or &lt;strong&gt;Berlin&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Risk &amp;amp; Fraud Prevention Analyst&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Berlin, Germany · Office-first · Permanent, full-time&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Global Fraud Prevention protects SumUp&#39;s banking products, from issued cards to cash in and cash out flows, keeping millions of merchants and consumers safe from financial crime. This role plays a key part in building stronger fraud observability and smarter decisioning for fast growing card issuing and banking volumes across the globe. Complex fraud data gets turned into practical controls here, working closely with fraud operations, data science, product, and engineering teams, as well as card payment networks, to stay ahead of evolving fraud patterns and comply with regulatory requirements in 38 active Sumup markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain fraud observability dashboards covering issued card, cash in, and cash out flows across merchant and consumer banking products&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and refine decision engine rules to catch fraud early without adding unnecessary friction for genuine customers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate fraud anomalies and turn findings into clear, actionable recommendations for fraud operations and engineering teams&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with data science and engineering teams to improve risk logic and explore new data sources and automation opportunities&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate PSD2, the upcoming PSD3, card scheme and other regulatory requirements into practical, workable controls&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share regular fraud performance updates with stakeholders across risk, compliance, and leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;The Engagement tribe sits at the heart of SumUp&#39;s merchant experience, responsible for the product surfaces that 4.3 million business owners interact with every day, from the information they see about their business to the actions they take to grow it. As our Senior Product Manager, you&#39;ll own the merchant facing SuperApp end to end, a rare individual contributor role spanning product strategy, UX quality, and squad delivery, on the single surface the wider product organisation depends on to build and ship effectively. If you&#39;re looking for a role where your product decisions have a direct impact on how millions of businesses run and scale every day, this is it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Own the end to end product experience of our SuperApp across iOS, Android and web dashboard, raising the bar on UX quality, information architecture, and navigation for the surfaces merchants rely on most&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Spot and execute activation, upsell, cross sell, and retention opportunities that measurably grow engagement and long term value for merchants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Shape the product strategy that makes the SuperApp an essential, everyday tool for small business owners running their business globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Act as the main point of contact for stakeholders across the business who depend on the SuperApp to reach merchants, partnering closely with design and data on priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Build strong working relationships across engineering, design, and commercial teams, turning direct merchant insight into a clear, prioritised roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll be great for this role if:&lt;/strong&gt;&l

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Run &amp;amp; Grow:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Run &amp;amp; Grow is where SumUp builds the platforms and capabilities that help merchants discover, join, use, and continue growing with our products. The tribe brings together engineering, product, design, and revenue operations teams around two connected goals: helping SumUp serve and retain merchants, and accelerating acquisition, activation, and engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work sits at the heart of SumUp’s growth engine. We turn complex challenges across merchant acquisition, identity, marketing technology, commercial systems, operations, risk, and compliance into reliable products and services that other teams can build on. The systems we create help SumUp move faster, make better decisions, and deliver a simpler experience to millions of small businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Joining Run &amp;amp; Grow means working on high-impact engineering problems with a broad view of the business. You’ll collaborate across disciplines and teams, shape the foundations behind important merchant journeys, and help create a more connected, scalable way for SumUp to run and grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
